{
  "id": "COMPOUND:21151 - PROTEIN:5702",
  "verbalization": "Schisanhenol B is implicated in the regulation of CCF-STTG1 through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Schisanhenol B acts as a target for multiple pathways, with the final target being CCF-STTG1. The first pathway involves Schisanhenol B directly targeting VMRC-LCP, which in turn targets CCF-STTG1. The second pathway links Schisanhenol B to MIP, which also targets CCF-STTG1, indicating a broader role in the regulation of this protein. The third pathway shows Schisanhenol B targeting MIP, which then directly targets CCF-STTG1, reinforcing the central role of Schisanhenol B in modulating this protein. The mechanisms appear to involve a cascade of molecular interactions, where Schisanhenol B influences the activity of MIP, which then affects CCF-STTG1. These findings suggest that Schisanhenol B may exert its biological effects through a complex network of molecular interactions, with CCF-STTG1 being a downstream effector. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between Schisanhenol B and CCF-STTG1, though the exact nature of the interactions remains to be fully elucidated.",
